<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Coscinodiscus wailesii Turing wavelength at 4.3 mm (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) (Coscinodiscus wailesii)",
        "Coscinodiscus wailesii Turing wavelength at 4.3 mm (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) faithfully reproduces Coscinodiscus wailesii morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Coscinodiscus wailesii specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Coscinodiscus wailesii" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A 4.3 mm frustule diameter.",
        "does_not_claim: A predecessor or successor chronospecies. The series is 1/1.",
        "does_not_claim: Nanometre readings of the SEM scale bars.",
        "does_not_claim: That the GIF copies micrograph pixels. cv_sim_similarity 84.8 is a feature-space score.",
        "does_not_claim: That the determinant minimizer selects the wavelength (it anti-correlates, r = -0.919).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Equal-diffusivity ablation and the disc clamp to (u0, v0).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Otsu segmentation of the six SEM panels and the KS distance on median-normalised diameters.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: sigma_+(q), k_c, the D_v sweep, the growth-rate estimator, and the 4.3 mm calibration.",
        "reported_in_source: Edwards et al. 2001: Holocene persistence in the north-east Atlantic from 1977.",
        "reported_in_source: Schmid and Volcani 1983: centrifugal proximal-to-distal morphogenesis of the C. wailesii valve, distal cribrum.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the trimolecular rate law. Spatial diffusion is a transfer into the Turing setting.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: wavelength selection by a linear instability of a homogeneous equilibrium.",
        "transfer_boundary: 4.3 mm is the assigned detail-scale wavelength. Retrieved abstracts do not state a valve diameter.",
        "transfer_boundary: Areolar spots stand in for the cohort form class. Pigment stripes are not claimed for this diatom." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Coscinodiscus wailesii; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: wavelength selection by a linear instability of a homogeneous equilibrium. | Schnakenberg 1979: the trimolecular rate law. Spatial diffusion is a transfer into the Turing setting. | Schmid and Volcani 1983: centrifugal proximal-to-distal morphogenesis of the C. wailesii valve, distal cribrum. | Edwards et al. 2001: Holocene persistence in the north-east Atlantic from 1977.; reconstructed_in_script: sigma_+(q), k_c, the D_v sweep, the growth-rate estimator, and the 4.3 mm calibration. | Equal-diffusivity ablation and the disc clamp to (u0, v0). | Otsu segmentation of the six SEM panels and the KS distance on median-normalised diameters.; transfer_boundary: 4.3 mm is the assigned detail-scale wavelength. Retrieved abstracts do not state a valve diameter. | Areolar spots stand in for the cohort form class. Pigment stripes are not claimed for this diatom.; does_not_claim: A 4.3 mm frustule diameter. | That the determinant minimizer selects the wavelength (it anti-correlates, r = -0.919). | Nanometre readings of the SEM scale bars. | A predecessor or successor chronospecies. The series is 1/1. | That the GIF copies micrograph pixels. cv_sim_similarity 84.8 is a feature-space score.]; phenomenon_size: 2.9 cm (0.02943 m, log10=-1.531 m, tier=7_organism_cm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 2.9 cm to 2.9 cm): 2.9 cm:diatom-frustule-phase-sep" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0025315401003654>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.0022-3646.1983.00387.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> ;
