    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps k_c = argmax sigma_+(k) calibrated to 4.3 mm at 0 Ma and replaces the headline residual. Two-time Fourier growth rates match lambda_sigma with Pearson r = 0.9997 and RMSE = 0.739 length units, against the pass-1 power-spectrum residual of r = 0.9899 and RMSE = 1.453. A --dv 48 probe returns lambda_sigma = 17.78 and lambda_growth = 18.56. The disc-clamped interior standard deviation is 0.719 against an ablation final standard deviation near 0.002. Upper-left SEM pitch is 10.15 px (n = 718, CV = 0.268) versus simulated pitch 14.06 px (CV = 0.086); KS = 0.317. The GIF remains 12 frames at 640×480 with cv_sim_similarity 84.8. Overall 91.0/100 (faithfulness 90.5, reproducibility 92.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 594009 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 249a0ac9549fd79e067741c1b3146ab5d9dc3fc7ea9ad62b976399680541937a (sha256 249a0ac9549fd79e067741c1b3146ab5d9dc3fc7ea9ad62b976399680541937a), spec_fingerprint 7caaeeacf26efa87e18b214d7dcc8b05a2350b3e3c52eadcca8cd98bd3b11f89. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7caaeeacf26efa87e18b214d7dcc8b05a2350b3e3c52eadcca8cd98bd3b11f89; artifact_sha256: 249a0ac9549fd79e067741c1b3146ab5d9dc3fc7ea9ad62b976399680541937a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0/coscinodiscus_wailesii_specimen.jpg=cf556dab9e116068..., datasets/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=e1fca8ca30c9782c..., datasets/coscinodiscus_wailesii_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=c6bf02023a4c27e5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: wavelength selection by a linear instability of a homogeneous equilibrium. | Schnakenberg 1979: the trimolecular rate law. Spatial diffusion is a transfer into the Turing setting. | Schmid and Volcani 1983: centrifugal proximal-to-distal morphogenesis of the C. wailesii valve, distal cribrum. | Edwards et al. 2001: Holocene persistence in the north-east Atlantic from 1977.; reconstructed_in_script: sigma_+(q), k_c, the D_v sweep, the growth-rate estimator, and the 4.3 mm calibration. | Equal-diffusivity ablation and the disc clamp to (u0, v0). | Otsu segmentation of the six SEM panels and the KS distance on median-normalised diameters.; transfer_boundary: 4.3 mm is the assigned detail-scale wavelength. Retrieved abstracts do not state a valve diameter. | Areolar spots stand in for the cohort form class. Pigment stripes are not claimed for this diatom.; does_not_claim: A 4.3 mm frustule diameter. | That the determinant minimizer selects the wavelength (it anti-correlates, r = -0.919). | Nanometre readings of the SEM scale bars. | A predecessor or successor chronospecies. The series is 1/1. | That the GIF copies micrograph pixels. cv_sim_similarity 84.8 is a feature-space score.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Growth-rate RMSE is 0.739 length units, a remaining systematic offset between the continuous argmax and the discrete ring estimator.",
        "remediation needed: SEM scale-bar labels were not transcribed to nanometres; panel pitches stay in pixels.",
        "remediation needed: The Lean 4 kernel was not executed here (no lean binary on the image). The proofs are decidable integer statements and remain to be checked by `lean` when a toolchain is present." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coscinodiscus-wailesii-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Coscinodiscus wailesii Turing wavelength at 4.3 mm (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "lambda_sigma increases across D_v in {16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 40, 48, 64}. The equal-diffusivity ablation decays (ratio 0.038) while the nominal branch grows. --dv 48 --probe-only returns lambda_sigma = 17.781 and lambda_growth = 18.563, longer than the D_v = 32 nominal, which is the monotonic control the parameter is supposed to have. Disc interior std is 0.719 against the near-zero ablation amplitude." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
